{"uid":"estorides_core/scope.py","name":"scope.py","qualname":"estorides_core/scope.py","kind":"module","file":"estorides_core/scope.py","line":1,"end_line":397,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"estorides_core.scope ===================== Bug-bounty scope classification.","description":"Takes the assets a passive run surfaces (hosts, IPs, CIDRs) and decides,\nfor each one, whether it is in-scope, out-of-scope, or unknown against a\nprogram's rules. Out-of-scope always wins so the operator never points\nactive tooling at an excluded asset — the fastest way to get removed from\na program.\n\nRule grammar (one rule per line, blank lines and `#` comments ignored):\n\n    *.example.com        wildcard host suffix (matches sub.example.com and example.com)\n    example.com          exact host\n    192.0.2.0/24         CIDR network (IPv4 or IPv6)\n    198.51.100.7         single IP address\n    re:^api[0-9]+\\.ex   regex (prefix ``re:``), matched against the raw asset\n\nA single rules file may carry both lists, divided by a line whose content\nis ``## out-of-scope`` (case-insensitive); rules above the divider are\nin-scope, rules below are out-of-scope. The two lists can also be supplied\nindependently when building a :class:`ScopeMatcher` directly.\n\nThe design is deliberately decoupled (SOLID): every grammar form is a\nsmall :class:`ScopeRule` with one ``matches`` method, rules are produced\nby an ordered list of detector factories (open/closed — add a form by\nappending one factory), and :class:`ScopeMatcher` only knows the\nout-beats-in precedence. No call site hard-codes a grammar.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["estorides_core/scope.py::IN_SCOPE","estorides_core/scope.py::OUT_OF_SCOPE","estorides_core/scope.py::UNKNOWN","estorides_core/scope.py::OUT_OF_SCOPE_DIVIDER","estorides_core/scope.py::normalise_asset","estorides_core/scope.py::is_ip","estorides_core/scope.py::ScopeRule","estorides_core/scope.py::WildcardRule","estorides_core/scope.py::ExactHostRule","estorides_core/scope.py::CidrRule","estorides_core/scope.py::RegexRule","estorides_core/scope.py::parse_rule","estorides_core/scope.py::parse_rules","estorides_core/scope.py::ScopeMatcher","estorides_core/scope.py::load_rules_file","estorides_core/scope.py::load_assets","estorides_core/scope.py::ScopeReport","estorides_core/scope.py::build_report","estorides_core/scope.py::write_flat_lists"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
